        <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white leading-tight">
          NACUAA Northern California San Francisco Chapter Founded: Expanding Bay Area Alumni Network & Advancing Cross-Chapter Synergy
        </h1>
        <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
          Expanding Bay Area alumni network, bridging commute distances, and deepening cross-chapter and cross-sector resource synergy
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Poem Banner Card -->
      <div class="p-6 md:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-gradient-to-br from-purple-950/60 via-slate-900 to-indigo-950/60 border border-purple-500/30 shadow-2xl text-center space-y-3">
        <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-purple-400 font-semibold flex items-center justify-center gap-2">
          <i class="fa-solid fa-feather-pointed"></i>
          <span>Double Ninth Eve · Dedication</span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-feather-pointed"></i>
        </div>
        <div class="text-base sm:text-lg md:text-xl font-medium text-purple-100 italic leading-relaxed space-y-1 py-1">
          <p>Autumn coolness graces San Francisco Bay as North American alumni gather together.</p>
          <p>From Silicon Valley, North Carolina to Washington, sister chapters embark on the voyage together.</p>
          <p>On the eighth night of the ninth lunar month in the Bing-Wu year, CSTU's lights illuminate the distance.</p>
          <p>Ascending tomorrow to watch the morning sunrise, tonight's spark weaves a splendid chapter.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Article Content -->
      <div class="text-slate-300 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed space-y-6">
        <p>
          On the evening of October 17, 2026, the Founding Ceremony of the North American Chinese University Alumni Alliance (NACUAA) Northern California San Francisco Chapter took place at California Science and Technology University (CSTU, 1601 McCarthy Blvd, Milpitas, CA), with simultaneous live streaming via Zoom. NACUAA President Sunny Chen officially announced the establishment of the San Francisco Chapter. Following the Silicon Valley Chapter, this marks another vital branch under NACUAA Northern California, signifying a strategic expansion and refinement of the Alliance's alumni network across the Greater San Francisco Bay Area.
        </p>

        <!-- Figure 1 -->
        <figure class="my-8 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 shadow-xl">
          <img 
            src="/images/2026-10-17-sf-founding/现场-联盟展架前四人合影.jpg" 
            alt="Figure: Attendees posing in front of the NACUAA banner" 
            class="w-full h-auto object-cover max-h-[550px]"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="p-3 text-center text-xs md:text-sm text-slate-400 bg-slate-950/70 border-t border-slate-800/80">
            Figure: Attendees posing in front of the NACUAA banner
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          The founding ceremony was presided over by Michael HUO, President of NACUAA Northern California. As event host, CSTU warmly welcomed guests and alumni. Shi Yi delivered welcoming remarks on behalf of California Science and Technology University, introducing the university's forthcoming Silicon Valley Robotics & AI Innovation Center. Shi Yi noted that CSTU prioritizes cutting-edge disciplines such as computer science, artificial intelligence, and data science. Drawing upon the Silicon Valley innovation ecosystem, the center will focus on AI, robotics, and embodied intelligence—building an integrated hub for technological innovation, enterprise incubation, product showcase, technology validation, industry partnership, and venture collaboration to accelerate research commercialization and global industry alignment. Subsequently, CSTU President Qin delivered remarks congratulating the establishment of the San Francisco Chapter. Highlighting the university's mission—student-centered, career-oriented, and high-tech focused—President Qin affirmed CSTU's commitment to supporting alumni and encouraged Bay Area graduates to unite and build collective strength.
        </p>

        <!-- Figure 2 & 3 Grid -->
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-8">
          <figure class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 shadow-xl flex flex-col justify-between">
            <img 
              src="/images/2026-10-17-sf-founding/秦校长-用户提供.jpg" 
              alt="Figure: CSTU President Qin delivering remarks at the founding ceremony" 
              class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <figcaption class="p-3 text-center text-xs md:text-sm text-slate-400 bg-slate-950/70 border-t border-slate-800/80">
              Figure: CSTU President Qin delivering remarks at the founding ceremony
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 shadow-xl flex flex-col justify-between">
            <img 
              src="/images/2026-10-17-sf-founding/Michael-HUO-本人提供.jpg" 
              alt="Figure: Portrait of NACUAA Northern California President Michael HUO (Archive Photo)" 
              class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <figcaption class="p-3 text-center text-xs md:text-sm text-slate-400 bg-slate-950/70 border-t border-slate-800/80">
              Figure: Portrait of NACUAA Northern California President Michael HUO (Archive Photo)
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-slate-800 flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-purple-500 rounded-full inline-block"></span>
          <span>Enhancing Bay Area Organizational Architecture: Dual-Track Synergy between Silicon Valley & San Francisco</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          NACUAA's development in Northern California is establishing an increasingly coherent regional layout. Alliance President Sunny Chen outlined the evolution of the organizational structure: as an inter-regional alumni alliance spanning 18 U.S. states and two Canadian cities, NACUAA has established a more specialized regional service framework in Northern California—the established Silicon Valley Chapter operates under NACUAA Northern California, and now the San Francisco Chapter is newly established under the regional umbrella. This structural enhancement matches the geographical distribution of alumni across diverse Bay Area communities, bridging commute distances and bringing event coordination and community engagement closer to where alumni live and work.
        </p>

        <p>
          Sunny Chen shared three expectations for the newly founded San Francisco Chapter: first, uniting alumni power to build a warm and supportive community; second, establishing a practical platform that creates substantive exchange and collaboration opportunities; and third, carrying forward the alumni spirit by actively serving the local community. Sunny Chen commended Northern California's executive execution, expressing heartfelt thanks to President Michael HUO for leading a vibrant team, as well as to senior leaders Dr. Qilei Peng and Jerry Zhang for their longstanding dedication and groundwork.
        </p>

        <p>
          Chairman of the Board Songhui Peng delivered warm congratulations on behalf of the NACUAA Board of Directors. Peng noted that, on top of the solid foundation built by Dr. Qilei Peng and core team members, the addition of President Michael HUO has substantially elevated team energy and event scale, exhibiting distinctive high-tech characteristics and community cohesion. He wished the San Francisco Chapter smooth sailing ahead.
        </p>

        <!-- Figure 4 -->
        <figure class="my-8 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 shadow-xl">
          <img 
            src="/images/2026-10-17-sf-founding/现场-查看会议材料与连线设备.jpg" 
            alt="Figure: Attendees reviewing ceremony materials and remote connection setup" 
            class="w-full h-auto object-cover max-h-[550px]"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="p-3 text-center text-xs md:text-sm text-slate-400 bg-slate-950/70 border-t border-slate-800/80">
            Figure: Attendees reviewing ceremony materials and remote connection setup
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-slate-800 flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-purple-500 rounded-full inline-block"></span>
          <span>Vision of the Inaugural Chapter President: Cultivating Alumni Community & Tech Entrepreneurship Resources</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          The assembly announced the appointment of Jane Zhang (widely known among alumni as "Doudou") as the inaugural president of the NACUAA Northern California San Francisco Chapter. Having studied at Columbia University, Jane has long focused on artificial intelligence, education, and tech entrepreneurship, actively participating in the Silicon Valley and San Francisco startup ecosystems.
        </p>

        <!-- Figure 5 -->
        <figure class="my-8 max-w-md mx-auto rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 shadow-xl">
          <img 
            src="/images/2026-10-17-sf-founding/张锦-Jane-油画风肖像-用户提供.jpg" 
            alt="Figure: Portrait of Inaugural San Francisco Chapter President Jane Zhang (Archive Photo)" 
            class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="p-3 text-center text-xs md:text-sm text-slate-400 bg-slate-950/70 border-t border-slate-800/80">
            Figure: Portrait of Inaugural San Francisco Chapter President Jane Zhang (Archive Photo)
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          In her inaugural address, Jane Zhang presented three primary initiatives: first, leveraging alumni ties to connect graduates living and working across San Francisco, progressively establishing a cohesive, supportive, and impactful alumni community; second, harnessing San Francisco's concentrated resources in technological innovation and entrepreneurship to serve as a bridge fostering inter-regional, inter-disciplinary collaborations and industry partnerships; third, maintaining open communication and synergy among sibling chapters so alumni benefit tangibly from shared regional resources. Jane emphasized that the new team will start from grassroots community building and systematically advance organizational mechanisms and local programming.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-slate-800 flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-purple-500 rounded-full inline-block"></span>
          <span>Cross-Chapter & Multi-Stakeholder Backing: Synergizing Quality Resources to Empower Emerging Leaders</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          The founding of the new chapter garnered enthusiastic support from established chapters, specialized clubs, and senior alumni leaders.
        </p>

        <p>
          Dr. Qilei Peng, Vice Chair of NACUAA and Founding President of the Silicon Valley Chapter, delivered congratulatory remarks celebrating the launch and applauding young Doudou on assuming the founding presidency. She looked forward to the San Francisco Chapter drawing more young alumni to explore, grow, and shine on the Alliance platform, developing into next-generation community leaders. Dr. Peng stated that as Silicon Valley Chapter founding president, she will collaborate closely with the San Francisco Chapter under President Huo's leadership to fortify Northern California's alumni foundation; while as NACUAA Vice Chair, she will champion resource sharing and inter-chapter collaboration, enabling the San Francisco Chapter to take flight standing upon the shoulders of the entire alliance.
        </p>

        <!-- Figure 6 -->
        <figure class="my-8 max-w-md mx-auto rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 shadow-xl">
          <img 
            src="/images/2026-10-17-sf-founding/彭启蕾-用户提供肖像.png" 
            alt="Figure: Portrait of Dr. Qilei Peng, NACUAA Vice Chair & Founding President of Silicon Valley Chapter (Archive Photo)" 
            class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="p-3 text-center text-xs md:text-sm text-slate-400 bg-slate-950/70 border-t border-slate-800/80">
            Figure: Portrait of Dr. Qilei Peng, NACUAA Vice Chair & Founding President of Silicon Valley Chapter (Archive Photo)
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Jerry Zhang, First President of NACUAA Northern California who laid the regional foundation, extended congratulations to President Jane and the new chapter. Jerry praised the team's cohesion and agility, noting that with his workplace situated between San Francisco and South Bay, he will actively assist San Francisco Chapter and club initiatives, providing logistical support and participating in sports, cultural, and tech lecture programs.
        </p>

