            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <p>
          NACUAA Vice Board Chair Ping He joined virtually to deliver remarks. As one of the founding members when NACUAA was established four years ago, Ping He expressed deep gratification in seeing Northern California unite youthful talent with fresh dynamism. Reaffirming her longstanding volunteer dedication to serving alumni, Ping He committed to supporting young leaders and looked forward to engaging in more in-person Northern California gatherings.
        </p>

        <p>
          Alliance Director Quan Li spoke on behalf of the AI Entrepreneurship Club, AI Media Creativity Club, Guandan Club, and Pickleball Club. Quan Li noted that these clubs regularly host activities across the Bay Area, including rotating pickleball games, Guandan friendly tournaments, and AI entrepreneurship sessions. With San Francisco being the global epicenter of AI innovation, the chapter's establishment provides a physical home in the core city. All clubs will open their speakers, startup networks, and recreational resources to the San Francisco Chapter, creating mutual synergy where "the chapter gathers momentum and clubs gain presence." Northern California also showcased an AI-generated commemorative video, demonstrating creative digital media applications in alumni community engagement.
        </p>

