            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <p>
          North Alpha Post Founder Guangyong Mao congratulated the chapter on behalf of media partners and North Carolina alumni. Mao shared his fondness for the San Francisco Bay Area and his admiration for California alumni's innovative drive and cultural vision. He noted that San Francisco embodies the historic heritage of Chinese-American perseverance; the new chapter not only tightens local alumni networks but also establishes an East-West Coast bridge for educational, technological, and cultural collaborations. North Alpha Post will fully leverage its media reach to chronicle alumni achievements and elevate Chinese community impact.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-slate-800 flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-purple-500 rounded-full inline-block"></span>
          <span>Community Engagement & Civic Participation: Encouraging Civic Service</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          The new chapter connects not only alumni and industries but also focuses on civic welfare and public service. Saratoga City Council Candidate Ping Li joined the gathering to congratulate the chapter.
        </p>

        <p>
          Ping Li recalled meeting and supporting Michael HUO during past civic activities, praising NACUAA for extending its focus beyond tech entrepreneurship into community welfare and public service. Ping Li expressed hopes for deeper future collaboration—continuing innovation in tech and AI while encouraging more Chinese Americans to engage with local public affairs, volunteer service, and city commissions, thereby amplifying civic voice and representation in local governance.
        </p>

