        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-slate-800 flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="w-2 h-6 bg-purple-500 rounded-full inline-block"></span>
          <span>Observations & Future Outlook: Moving from Announcement to Sustainable Operations</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          The establishment of the San Francisco Chapter completes NACUAA's strategic organizational presence in Northern California's core metropolitan area. Participating representatives highlighted that realizing the chapter's vision depends on the execution quality of day-to-day operations and alumni services.
        </p>

        <p>
          Moving forward, the San Francisco Chapter will establish its local communications network, coordinate core volunteer teams, and plan initial local activities. Alumni can stay updated via the NACUAA Northern California <a href="https://norcal.nacuaa.ai/posts/2026-10-17-nacuaa-san-francisco-chapter-founding-ceremony/" class="text-purple-400 underline hover:text-purple-300">Official Event Portal</a>.
